I found the REAL issue 👍

Your problem is NOT in btn_Submit.

The problem is in:

txt_Comment.OnChange


---

🎯 WHY IT FAILS

Your txt_Comment.OnChange currently does this:

RemoveIf(colAnswers,...)
Collect(colAnswers,...)

❌ This is WRONG for optional comments.

Because when you type comment:

it removes existing radio answer

then re-adds only ONE record

causing CountRows(colAnswers) mismatch



---

🧠 EXAMPLE

You have:

2 suppliers × 4 questions = 8 answers


---

After radio selection

CountRows(colAnswers) = 8 ✅


---

Then typing comment

Your code removes/recollects:

ONLY ONE QUESTION RECORD

Now collection becomes inconsistent ❌


---

✅ FIX (IMPORTANT)

Since comments are OPTIONAL:

DO NOT TOUCH colAnswers from txt_Comment


---

🎯 CONTROL TO UPDATE

Update:

txt_Comment

Property:

OnChange


---

✅ REPLACE EVERYTHING WITH THIS

Blank()

OR simply leave it empty.


---

🚨 VERY IMPORTANT

DELETE this entire old code from txt_Comment.OnChange:

With(
    {
        supplierId: Gallery_Suppliers_New.Selected.ID,
        supplierName: Gallery_Suppliers_New.Selected.Title,
        questionId: ThisItem.ID,
        questionTitle: ThisItem.Title
    },

    RemoveIf(
        colAnswers,
        SupplierID = supplierId &&
        QuestionID = questionId
    );

    Collect(
        colAnswers,
        {
            SupplierID: supplierId,
            SupplierName: supplierName,
            QuestionID: questionId,
            QuestionTitle: questionTitle,
            Score: Radio_Score_New.Selected.Value,
            Comment: Self.Text
        }
    )
)

❌ REMOVE IT COMPLETELY


---

✅ WHY THIS FIXES IT

Now:

colAnswers = radio answers ONLY

Comments:

handled separately during submit

Exactly what you want 👍


